irc-serve (0.8.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Federation-integration release: actor echo on forwarded state changes
  * (#558), inbound S-verb client emission (#559), SASL 903-908 numerics
  * (#560), remote KICK/MODE/WHOIS targets (#606/#607), QUIT/NICK echo
  * (#609), departure propagation (#608), shutdown flush (#591), live
  * staging-verified two-node mesh. No wire change since 0.2.0.

 -- TheFirstIstari <euphonium.ashe.f@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

irc-serve (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 4.3 wire extension (#563): SJOIN carries user+host; SSETNAME, SAWAY and
  * SINVITE federate realname, away and invite notify across peer links.
  * FEDERATE still requires an exact version match, so 0.1.x nodes refuse
  * 0.2.0 links at the handshake instead of misparsing the new shapes.

 -- TheFirstIstari <euphonium.ashe.f@gmail.com>  Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

irc-serve (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: federated modern-spec IRC server in C.
  * Performance-first, minimal memory footprint (<10MB base per node).
  * TDD framework with observable contracts per protocol/regression/test.
  * CI: ci_testExpected, ci_benchmarkExpected, ci_complianceExpected.

